1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nc6 5. Nb5 d6 6. c4 Nf6 7. N1c3 a6 8. Na3
Be7 9. Be2 O-O 10. O-O b6 11. Be3 Ne5 12. f4 Ned7 13. Bf3 Bb7 14. Qe2 Qc7 15.
Rac1 Rfe8 16. Rfd1 Rac8 17. g4 h6 18. h4 Nh7 19. Qh2 g5 {Played with great
emphasis by the Russian, as if saying: "Now see if you can mate me on the
h-file!"} 20. hxg5 hxg5 21. f5 Bf8 22. Kf2 Ndf6 23. Rh1 Bg7 24. Qg2 Qe7 25.
Rce1 exf5 26. exf5 Bxf3 27. Qxf3 Ne4+ 28. Nxe4 Qxe4 29. Qxe4 Rxe4 30. Kf3 Rce8
31. b3 Bc3 {Black's pieces have come to life.} 32. Re2 Nf6 33. Nc2 {Black
offered a draw but was turned down. In response he lit a cigarette.} d5 34. Rg2
dxc4 35. Bxg5 cxb3 36. axb3 Nd7 37. Rgh2 Bg7 38. Rd1 Nf6 39. Bf4 {Now, surely,
the attack is about to break through with g5 coming. The wily veteran plays
that ungainly knight move again - and wins a thousand pounds!} Nh7 $1 40. g5 $4
(40. Rg2 $16) 40... Rxf4+ $1 41. Kxf4 Be5+ 42. Kg4 Bxh2 43. Rd4 Bg1 44. Rd2 Bc5
45. Kh5 Re5 46. Rd8+ Nf8 47. Kg4 Re2 {Source: bulletin; BCM, February 1991, p55
} 0-1

